# Product

Walkthrough: AWS IoT Greengrass V2 **greenhouse** lab on an Intel NUC6CAY **core**
with ESP32-S3 **client devices** (zones), closed-loop sense → actuate. Maps AWS
marketing concepts onto real hardware. NUC chosen because one was already on hand.
Starlight docs. AWS CLI only — no Terraform, no provision/deploy wrappers.

## Outcomes

- Core vs client (certs, roles, discovery) is explicit; SPOF called out vs direct IoT.
- Nucleus on Ubuntu 24.04 (NUC6CAY); ESP32-S3 as client devices, not second cores.
- Real sense→actuate loop (button → RGB) plus chip-temperature telemetry.
- Act 2 (Wire into AWS) as a continuous demo: S3 artifact → cloud deploy (+ LogManager),
  IoT rules → S3 / DynamoDB / CloudWatch alarm → SNS → Lambda → cloud→edge command,
  SageMaker → ONNX inference on the core (not Edge Manager).
- Teardown of every resource, last.

## Non-goals (v1)

Greengrass V1, Terraform/CDK, CI-driven AWS apply, EC2-as-edge happy path,
Edge Manager, Stream Manager / ESP32 OTA hands-on, Mosquitto-only lab, Docker lab,
high-level pages without runnable CLI.

Details: `.kiro/steering/product.md`, `AGENTS.md`.
